egrity**\n- **Lock check only compares length** (`harness/src/verify.ts:272`). It checks that the local lock has the same length as the committed one, not the same content. I edited a dev fixture and rewrote the lock, and both integrity checks then returned no problems, so verify would score a tampered evaluator.\n- **Scores come from a different lock.** The headline run was made under lock `0cf3b94b0704`, but the committed lock hashes to `ccfca18be06f`. The published scores can't be reproduced from the committed evaluator.\n- **Lock coverage has gaps.** It doesn't hash the container's `Dockerfile`, `harness/test/` or `holdout-seed.json`. I changed all three and the lock check still passed.\n\n**Statistics**\n- **Bounds are ten times too small** (`harness/src/fidelity.ts:67`). The formatter multiplies by 10 instead of 100. My verify run printed 0.06 % for the 473/473 batch, where the correct figure is 0.63 %. This also makes `npm run check` fail.\n- **Spent batch reported as clean.** The fidelity report lists the spent holdout batch 1 as a second clean 473/473 measurement, with bounds.\n- **Hash-split holdout isn't clean.** It is reported as clean, but it includes cases that `GAPS.md` itself calls spent or informed (`d-month-to-year`, `rand-005`, `fresh-007`, `t-*`, `u-*`).\n- **Wrong plan for the policy check.** The \"policy changed since the plan\" check always reads batch 1's plan, so it is wrong for batch 2.\n\n**Isolation**\n- **Guard fails open** (`guard-oracle.sh:8`). On any internal error it exits 1, which lets the tool call through. I reproduced this with invalid JSON input and with `jq` missing.\n- **Web access isn't guarded.** The hook isn't attached to WebFetch, so its block on code hosts never runs. Yet the sandbox grants WebFetch and the container has network access.\n- **Holdout inputs are visible.** The sandbox includes `probes.ts` with its fixed seeds and the split function, so a builder can list exactly which inputs are scored as holdout. Only the 